docs\WORKFLOW.md:198:Owner baseline: State Request **CLOSED / PASS**, both local databases at 0002, working DEVELOPMENT launcher/F2 and pgAdmin, Git checkpoint `f95db80`. Notification source/offline work supersedes historical notification deferral statements. No live database access/migration, real approval/authorization issuance, provider setup, production email, separate administration system or Git staging/commit/push is part of this task.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:202:The existing `oaf_website.state_requests.create_app(...)` now registers `/api/notifications/session`, POST `/api/notifications`, and POST `/api/notifications/unsubscribe` alongside the preserved State Request routes, using the same verified runtime engine and protected persistent key with a separate signing domain. Startup performs no migrations or schema creation. The explicit public-file allowlist adds `assets/notifications.js`; DEVELOPMENT's F2 launcher and its 0002 startup checks remain unchanged. Subscription writes return a sanitized unavailable response until the separately authorized 0003 migration is applied.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:208:Offline validation adds `tests/test_notifications.py` and `tests/test_notification_migration.py` to the ten-file suite, preserving `-B`, the dedicated website interpreter, empty pytest plugin/options settings and `-p migration_offline`. Select all twelve test files explicitly. Synthetic operational approvals/authorizations remain restricted to test temporary directories; they are not owner issuance. Browser checks use `..\GraManna\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B tests/notification_browser_check.py` and the existing State Request browser check, with intercepted requests and no database access or GraManna repository edits.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:210:Deterministic autonomy review: fixed server eligibility, validation, consent, atomic duplicate suppression, permanent lifecycle receipts, signature verification, withdrawal, sanitization and idempotent repeat rules; no AI or manual per-submission decision. Foundation announcement/geographic approval, future delivery/verification and separately gated migration/deployment remain administrative controls. Offline model/Chromium results do not establish PostgreSQL catalog/ACL/concurrency semantics or deployed readiness.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:214:Source validation results: all twelve offline regression files passed **1,204 tests** in **58.06 seconds**, with zero unexpected external-access attempts. The focused notification/migration/authorization run passed **248 tests**. Notification and preserved State Request intercepted Chromium checks passed at **1280px and 390px**, with zero page errors or external requests. Revision 0001 and 0002 bytes match HEAD; shared CSS and State Request JavaScript are unchanged. Pre-existing README, VS Code, DEVELOPMENT launcher and prerequisite-helper changes were preserved. Staging remains empty. These results establish tested source/model/UI behavior only; no live PostgreSQL or production readiness is claimed.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:216:Task file inventory: `gramanna.html`, `assets/notifications.js`; `oaf_website/notifications.py`, `oaf_website/notification_schema.py`, `oaf_website/notification_validation.py`, `oaf_website/state_requests.py`, `oaf_website/local_testing.py`; `migrations/versions/0003_notifications.py`, `migrations/manifest.json`, `oaf_website/migration_validation.py`, `oaf_website/migration_authority.py`; `tests/test_notifications.py`, `tests/test_notification_migration.py`, `tests/notification_browser_check.py`, `tests/migration_offline.py`, `tests/test_migration_artifacts.py`, `tests/test_migration_authorization.py`, `tests/state_request_browser_check.py`; `docs/WEBSITE_PLAN.md`, `docs/WORKFLOW.md`. No task edits to pre-existing owner changes or approved revisions were made.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:220:Both baseline migrations are CLOSED / PASS per the owner. State Request implementation and focused offline validation are authorized; prior baseline-only/feature-deferral language is historical for this task. Preserve owner changes and all Stage 5 controls. No live database, credentials, real audit/approval/authorization records, paid provisioning, or Git staging/commit/push are authorized.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:222:The supported new transition is exactly `0001_migration_baseline -> 0002_state_requests`; a separately authorized no-op may start at 0002. A `base -> 0002` jump, downgrade, stamp, or multi-revision execution remains prohibited. Revision 0001 stays unchanged. Matching hashes remain integrity evidence, not artifact approval. New artifact hashes do not reuse baseline execution authorizations or rewrite old evidence.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:224:Offline checks add `tests/test_state_requests.py` and `tests/test_state_request_migration.py` to the existing eight explicitly selected files with the same early isolation plugin and website interpreter. Tests use Flask's in-process client, compiled PostgreSQL SQL, temporary synthetic approval evidence and a transactional database model. These checks cannot establish actual PostgreSQL concurrency, catalog/ACL semantics or browser-cookie behavior.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:236:**Current scope supersedes historical Stage 1 status statements below.** The four policies A-D are owner-approved. Stage 4C development/testing migrators are CLOSED / DELIVERED / PASS as reported by the owner; this source task does not repeat live verification. Stage 5 operational adapter source and offline validation are authorized. Independent artifact approval is **pending**; owner-issued execution authorization is **pending**; live migration execution is **not authorized**. No real authorization record is issued by this task. No live credentials, PostgreSQL changes, package installation, staging, commits, or pushes are authorized.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:243:`FileOperationalAuthority` implements the existing `OperationalAuthority.authorize(request, run_id, artifacts) -> AuditSink` contract. The exact class is registered in `_OPERATIONAL_ADAPTER_TYPES`; protocol-shaped objects and subclasses cannot authorize work. The migration CLI accepts only an existing `--authorization-id`. Direct runner calls require the same concrete authority, and Alembic requires the runner's single-use context and the authority's actual request/run/sink binding. There is no fallback engine or direct Alembic execution permission. Repository-only `plan` performs integrity checks and grants no execution authority.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:245:The transition remains `base -> 0001_migration_baseline`, with the revision unchanged and metadata-only. A no-op must separately authorize `expected_start=0001_migration_baseline`; an authorization for `base` cannot silently adopt an already-applied state. Testing is the first future live target. Development requires its own authorization and a prerequisite approval citing a successful testing baseline validation run for the same artifact hashes. Existing environment/DB/role matching, exact WinVault targets, SCRAM expectations, owner assumption, schema-qualified metadata, transaction, lock, timeout, drift, and manifest checks remain required.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:249:These are source interface instructions for a later separately authorized owner action, not permission to create real approvals or execute now. All operational records stay outside Git in MigrationAudit. The issuer is `python -m oaf_website.migration_authority issue --specification <absolute-owner-specification-path> --owner-issue`; it never connects to PostgreSQL or reads credentials. It returns a UUID only after completed issuance is published; a readable authorization payload alone cannot be consumed. Publication is the completion point even if the process stops before delivering its response; never blindly reissue after an interrupted response. `python -m oaf_website.migrate` uses `--authorization-id <issued-uuid>` with its existing explicit request arguments. Do not run a live upgrade/downgrade during source validation.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:265:Run the dedicated website `.venv` interpreter with `PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1`, empty `PYTEST_ADDOPTS`/`PYTEST_PLUGINS`, repository plus tests on `PYTHONPATH`, and `-B -m pytest -p migration_offline -q`. Explicitly select all eight test files: `tests/test_database_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_config.py`, `tests/test_migration_artifacts.py`, `tests/test_migration_authorization.py`, `tests/test_migration_catalog.py`, `tests/test_migration_runner.py`, `tests/test_migration_provenance.py`, and `tests/test_migration_operational.py`. The plugin blocks credential/network/database access before collection, guards real BootstrapAudit file reads, and redirects operational file tests to temporary directories. Approval and authorization records in tests are synthetic. No live Alembic operation or real owner issuance is part of these checks.
docs\WORKFLOW.md:271:The following Stage 1 approval/status and unresolved-policy wording is preserved as checkpoint history. For migration policies, source implementation, Stage 4C delivery, and the current authorization boundary, the Stage 5 entry above is controlling; it does not reopen policies A-D or grant live execution.
