docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:214:The existing runtime configuration loader remains restricted to runtime accounts. Migration identities require their own separate, fail-closed configuration path using the preserved Windows Credential Manager backend and selected matching credential reference. Alembic `env.py` must not construct a fallback engine; Flask startup must never run migrations.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:216:The initial metadata-only revision is `0001_migration_baseline`. It establishes Alembic revision tracking under the matching schema owner, without creating Request Your State feature tables or endpoints and without runtime privileges on version metadata.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:225:The standardized suffix is plural: `/Migrations`. These are approved design identities; migration credentials have **NOT been provisioned**. Existing runtime service references in the configuration foundation remain separate. Preserve Windows Credential Manager and the same-user access limitation documented in `WORKFLOW.md`; do not embed passwords in documentation or examples. Future production credentials require separate authorization and protection.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:234:2. Verify the connected database and authenticated migrator; explicitly assume and verify the matching schema owner for migration-managed DDL. Enforce a controlled `search_path` for the intended application schema and qualified object access without relying on caller/session defaults or writable unintended schemas.
