docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:244:Initially prohibit nontransactional migration operations, revision-controlled commits, autocommit blocks, ordinary downgrade, stamp, automatic destructive repair, and blind retries after uncertain commits. Authorized administrative intervention remains appropriate for exceptional changes, destructive recovery, ownership corrections, and unexplained drift.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:248:**UNRESOLVED OPERATIONAL PREREQUISITES:** Before seeking migration execution authorization, verify the existing administrator authentication/authority and PostgreSQL 17 grantor path; separately authorize/provision migration credentials; validate the Alembic pin and artifact manifest approval process; and establish and approve advisory-lock scope/lifetime, controlled search-path details, timeout enforcement, postcondition/drift checks, and verified recovery/uncertain-commit procedures.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:250:Establish and owner-approve the precise audit destination, retention policy, failed-write behavior, and operational evidence procedure before migration execution is authorized. Follow the sanitized evidence categories, exclusions, independent review, and same-account log limitations in `WORKFLOW.md`. Raw operational logs stay outside Git; only independently reviewed, sanitized validation evidence may accompany an authorized Git checkpoint. Audit persistence is not implemented; no retention period or new paid logging service is approved.
